From b69981957c6070357e5ec6e33ef951085ab6864a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:53:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/44] demux: ttml: move the demux watermark when seeking

Demux() emits cues while their time is at or below i_next_demux_time and
otherwise only ever advances it, an eighth of a second per pass. Seeking
moved times.i_current but left the watermark where playback had reached,
so a seek backwards - including the seek to the start that repeats a file
- left every remaining cue at or below it. The next pass emitted the lot
in one go, timestamped in the past.

Set it to the requested time, as the webvtt and subtitle demuxers do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/ttml.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/ttml.c b/modules/demux/ttml.c
index 8e5471cb46..91b11b84b2 100644
--- a/modules/demux/ttml.c
+++ b/modules/demux/ttml.c
@@ -243,6 +243,9 @@ static int Control( demux_t* p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
                                                             p_sys->times.i_count, t, &b );
                 p_sys->times.i_current = i_index;
                 p_sys->b_first_time = true;
+                /* Demux() only ever advances this; leaving it behind would
+                 * flush every remaining cue at once. */
+                p_sys->i_next_demux_time = i64 - VLC_TICK_0;
                 return VLC_SUCCESS;
             }
             break;
@@ -287,6 +290,9 @@ static int Control( demux_t* p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
                                                             p_sys->times.i_count, t, &b );
                 p_sys->times.i_current = i_index;
                 p_sys->b_first_time = true;
+                /* Demux() only ever advances this; leaving it behind would
+                 * flush every remaining cue at once. */
+                p_sys->i_next_demux_time = i64;
                 return VLC_SUCCESS;
             }
             break;
